Description: Advantech Board Support Package (BSP) registry manager
 bsp-registry-tools manages Yocto BSP registries: it resolves BSP
 presets, fetches layer repositories via kas and drives bitbake builds.
 .
 The package provides:
  - bsp: the main CLI (build, gather, flash, registry management)
  - bsp-explorer: an interactive TUI registry explorer
  - bsp-explorer-web: the TUI served in a browser (textual-serve)
  - bsp server: a REST + GraphQL HTTP API (FastAPI/Strawberry)
  - bsp-mcp: an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server for AI agents
  - systemd service units for the servers (disabled by default)
 .
 All Python dependencies (server, gui, mcp, completions and deploy
 extras, including kas) are bundled in a self-contained virtualenv
 under /opt/venvs/bsp-registry-tools; only the system Python
 interpreter of the matching distribution release is required at
 runtime. The "report" extra (weasyprint) is not bundled because it
 needs system pango/cairo libraries; install it into the venv with
 /opt/venvs/bsp-registry-tools/bin/pip install 'bsp-registry-tools[report]'
 after installing the suggested pango packages.
